ticket.bug:
When creating a Carrier linked to a CarrierModule, the method CarrierModule::getOrderShippingCost() is failing because the instance does not have an id_carrier (null).

I traced back the problem to this code in CartCore :

```
if (!$module->id_carrier) {
    $module->id_carrier = $carrier->id;
}
```

Which was before :

```
if ($module->id_carrier) {
    $module->id_carrier = $carrier->id;
}
```

After migration of module configuration to symfony, multilanguage switchers are broken.

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b34bc41-a3ce-4bac-ab14-58c2fbafce97)

Following code in `admin.js` relies on a variable that was forgotten.

```js
function changeEmployeeLanguage()
{
  if (typeof allowEmployeeFormLang !== 'undefined' && allowEmployeeFormLang)
    for (var key in languages) {
      if (id_language === languages[key]['id_lang']) {
        $.post(changeFormLanguageUrl, {
          language_iso_code: languages[key]['iso_code']
        });

        break;
      }
    }
}
```

It expects this code that is present now only in legacy AdminController. It must be also added to the symfony page.

```php
Media::addJsDef([
            'changeFormLanguageUrl' => $this->context->link->getAdminLink(
                'AdminEmployees',
                true,
                [],
                ['action' => 'formLanguage']
            ),
        ]);
```

Ping @jolelievre @tleon

ticket.expected:
Context::getContext()->cookie->testmessage = 'something in the cookie';
and
unset(Context::getContext()->cookie->testmessage);
must work.

Ping @jolelievre @tleon

